    {
      "body": "## Claude Code Review\n\nThis pull request is from a fork — automated review is disabled. A repository maintainer can comment `@claude review` to run a one-time review.",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/53244#pullrequestreview-4991592260",
      "id": 4991592260,
      "state": "COMMENTED",
      "submitted_at": "2026-08-21T09:00:21Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "claude[bot]"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Thanks for the contribution, it's a clear improvement over the current state. Sadly it's not a full fix. And I think that with the information currently available it can't be fixed fully.\n\nWhen two requests share an X-Request-Id, renewing only the first match can expire a live lease. Renewing all of them can keep stale ones alive while the id keeps being reused.\n\nC1 and C4 from #48633 have the same underlying problem. They need an extra signal that reliably identifies the dispatched request (from the router) to be fixed without other side effects.\n\nI opened a discussion on Slack [here](https://vllm-dev.slack.com/archives/C0A9AAG7QR2/p1790760867615409) on how best to introduce that signal.\n\nThe question for this PR is whether we merge it as a temporary improvement or wait for that decision to fix these bugs together. I'd leave that to @NickLucche.\n\nIf we merge it as a temporary improvement, I'd suggest moving the push-only logic from base_scheduler.py and base_worker.py into push_scheduler.py and push_worker.py.",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/53244#pullrequestreview-5367107076",
      "id": 5367107076,
      "state": "COMMENTED",
